            <ArticleTitle>Hybrid imaging of musculoskeletal infections.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.23736/S1824-4785.17.03045-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review article highlights the role of radiological and nuclear medicine techniques in diagnosis of musculoskeletal infections with particular regard to hybrid imaging of osteomyelitis, prosthetic joint infections, sternal infections and spine infections. Authors conclude on the complementary role of the several techniques with indications for an appropriate diagnostic flow chart, in the light of the recent EANM guidelines on infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
